+## v4 (final, lead)
+
+v4 = v3 with the two v3 load workarounds **reverted** (articles_controller.rb#create and article_commit.rb are
+byte-identical to v2 again) and ExportsController simplified (w21):
+
+- The v3 crash was a Spinel code-generation bug, now fixed in the toolchain: arguments of a call on a dynamically
+  typed receiver (and the result temp of a no-else `(expr if cond)`) were not registered as GC roots
+  (`spinel-poly-dispatch-arg-roots.patch`, root-caused by the lead's Claude subagent c01; see
+  .work/ruby-compile/spinel-spike/workers/c01-spinel-lifetime). With it, the original merged-Hash create path survives
+  ~50,000 creates under the benchmark load with zero failures (lead/crash/v4a, v4b).
+- `app/controllers/exports_controller.rb`: the explicit integer-serialization regex/`to_i` is removed; roundhouse patch 74
+  now gives Rails' out-of-range / nonnumeric integer predicate semantics generally (huge IDs -> no match -> 404).
+  The only remaining delta in this file is the direct `user_id` query (association `find_by` lowering still derives a
+  nonexistent `current_user_id`) plus `param(:id)`.
+
+v4 acceptance: compiled production gate exit 0 (prod/production-gate-v4-1.log); common reviewer probe 21/21 contract,
+3/3 quality (probe/compiled-v4-common-http.json); Rails production gate exit 0 (gates/v4-rails-production.log); Rails
+db:prepare, Zeitwerk, RuboCop (51 files, no offenses), 21 tests / 115 assertions (gates/v4-rails-dev).
+Behavioral difference removed in v4: huge numeric export/comment IDs now return 404 as in Rails.
+
+
+## v5 (upstream heads, 2026-10-02)
+
+v5 = v4 with four workarounds **reverted**, built with Roundhouse `main` @ `5bbc4765` + 11 local patches and
+Spinel `master` @ `d2c20df0b` with no local patch (workers: `SPINEL_WORKERS=4` in the production image).
+Each revert was tried alone on v4 and kept only when the compiled production gate stayed green; the
+evidence is in the v5 package, `results/ruby-compile/roundhouse-spinel-conduit-pg-20261002/`
+(README.md, evidence/gates/reverts, evidence/edge).
+
+- `app/services/live_rooms.rb`: **byte-identical to the reference again** (`Room = Struct.new(:lock, :members)`,
+  `Room.new(Mutex.new, {})`). Fixed upstream by matz/spinel#6580 (a Struct member named like a Struct method reads
+  the member; `attr_reader :members` read out of a container). The v2 entry for this file no longer applies.
+  The nil-seeded `{nil => 0}` hash is gone; socket-keyed membership, presence, updates, revocation and the
+  100-member cap were checked on the compiled build.
+- `app/controllers/articles_controller.rb#create`: `input.fetch("tagList", [])` replaces the `key?` workaround.
+  Fixed upstream by matz/spinel#6654 (`fetch` with an empty `[]`/`{}` default on a boxed Hash). The remaining
+  delta in this file is the typed JSON body (string keys, `permitted`, no `to_unsafe_h`).
+- `app/controllers/users_controller.rb#update`: `@current_user.update!(permitted(object!(:user), %i[...]))`
+  replaces the direct-writer loop. Fixed upstream by matz/spinel#6572 (a call converted into an `--rbs` Hash
+  parameter keeps its result). The reference's `object!(:user).permit(...)` is still blocked by the typed-JSON
+  body gap (no `permit` on the parsed Hash: every update answers 500) and the generated `update!` still reads
+  only Symbol keys (a String-keyed Hash saves nothing, silently), so the `permitted` helper stays.
+  An edge differential of 24 update bodies (nil, numbers, booleans, Hash/Array values, unknown keys,
+  unwrapped bodies, taken/blank names, password changes) gave the same responses as v4.
+- `app/controllers/users_controller.rb#login` and `application_controller.rb`: `input[field.to_s].blank?`
+  replaces the `blank_value?` helper, which is deleted. Roundhouse lowers an untyped `blank?` to
+  `ActiveSupport.blank?` (`lower::blank`, already before the v4 base); it uses the same `to_s.strip`, so the
+  documented Unicode-whitespace difference from Rails `blank?` remains, now in the runtime rather than the app.
+
+Tried and **not** kept (the workaround stays):
+- `app/services/login_throttle.rb`, reference form: every failed login answers 500
+  (`NoMethodError: undefined method 'reject!' for an instance of Array`). Restoring only `reject!` gives the same 500;
+  restoring only the raise inside `synchronize` loses the 429 (500 in the gate, no response in a direct probe).
+  Needs the rest of the Spinel synchronize/exception stack (open: matz/spinel#7102, #7136, #7155 and the
+  unopened splits).
+- `application_controller.rb#article_json`, reference `association(:author).loaded?`: compiles, then every article
+  read answers 500 (no `association` on the compiled model). No upstream fix yet.
+
+v5 acceptance: see `results/ruby-compile/roundhouse-spinel-conduit-pg-20261002/README.md`.
